# implements-port slice 1 under --walk-methods: the natively supported call of a callable formal
# with arguments (unit_cf_call_args.lm2) is outside the walkable subset (l2_rw_may) and is refused,
# located -- the walker does not silently leave it native (checkpoint 2-6, row 234: "same in
# native and walker" is an explicit refusal here, REVIEW 9327b65).
fn: intToInt (int: x) int
end: intToInt
fn: inc (int: x) int
    return: x + 1
end: inc
fn: apply (intToInt: op; int: value) int
    return: op(value)
end: apply
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: apply(inc, 6); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
